In order to hack into your neighbor's internet to use their wifi, you will need to set up a fake Wi-Fi network. First, determine the frequency of your neighbor’s router. If your neighbor uses a router that runs on 2.4GHz or 5GHz band, you can simply use software programs such as Network Auditor to sniff out what frequency is being used by the router. Once you have gathered the information, create a new network using the same settings as that of your neighbor’s router. Once completed, use another device with varying credentials in order to connect into the fake network and gain access to your neighbor’s internet connection.
